abstract: >-
  The IRIS Gate protocol is a cross-architecture critique framework for
  using language models from different architectures as peer reviewers
  during hypothesis development. The protocol formalizes a four-step
  pipeline (claim surfacing, cross-architecture critique, structural
  decomposition, citation and standing verification) and documents
  the methodology that lets independent model architectures converge
  on or diverge from a working claim. Includes epistemic humility
  classification (TRUST/VERIFY/OVERRIDE) for reliability triage.
